zune-jpeg: let an incremental decode retry when the DNL segment is not visible yet

`decode_mcu_ycbcr_baseline_inner` (mcu.rs) looks for the DNL marker after the
scan of a height-0 image with `get_marker`, and turned every error into the
hard error "DNL marker expected (SOF height was 0) but not found in scan
data". When an incremental caller has only supplied data up to (or just past
the 0xFF of) the DNL segment, `get_marker` fails with a recoverable EOF, and
the decode failed for good although the next chunk carries the DNL; a
one-shot decode of the same bytes succeeds. Pass the recoverable EOF through
when the decoder is in incremental mode and the input is not marked complete
(new helper `scan_eof_is_retryable`, the incremental half of
`scan_eof_is_error`); one-shot and final-input decodes keep the hard error.
Includes a regression test (tests/incremental_resume.rs, needs `arith`).

Not fixed upstream as of zune-image 2cdbbf5.
Upstream: none found.

